# identity.baseline -- the string comparisons of two runtime operands that
# were in src/ when the identifier-comparison lint landed, at 6e2dca123.
#
# This is a ratchet, not a list of defects.  tests/lint/identity.lint says why
# the lint cannot classify a site: measured at 6e2dca123 over the 274 records
# this file then held, 95 are identity comparisons of a name a deck wrote and
# 171 are comparisons of a word the language defines or of text that is not an
# identifier at all.  The lint has no opinion about which is which.  What it
# enforces is that the set does not change without someone saying so.
#
# The count is the measurement's, not this file's, and the two part company as
# entries leave.  Entries removed since:
#
#   src/frontend/subckt.c  eq_substr(name, name_end, table[i].t_old)
#       gettrans()'s subcircuit formal pin lookup, which was one of the 95 and
#       is doc/codex/issues/0049: byte-exact under preserve, where two
#       spellings of one pin are one pin, so a body that spelled a pin in the
#       other case got a silently disconnected subcircuit.  It calls
#       eq_substr_id() now, which is not a comparator this lint looks for.
#       Removed 2026-08-11 with doc/claude/decisions/0012.  273 records.
#
#   src/frontend/define.c  eq(name, udf->ud_name)              (twice)
#   src/frontend/define.c  eq(wlist->wl_word, udf->ud_name)
#   src/frontend/define.c  eqc(ft_funcs[i].fu_name, tbuf)
#       ft_substdef(), prdefs() and com_undefine() are the three resolutions
#       of a user-defined function name, and doc/codex/issues/0020 gap 2:
#       byte-exact, so a function answered only to the spelling it was
#       defined with, and the shipped vm/vp/vdb went with it.  All three call
#       udf_name_eq() now.  The fourth, com_define()'s predefined-function
#       check, is unchanged code: it is a keyword test and now says so in a
#       `case-lint:` comment, which is decision 4's second way out and a
#       third way for an entry to leave -- not by the comparison leaving, but
#       by its being classified where it stands.
#       Removed 2026-08-11 with doc/claude/decisions/0013.  269 records.
#
#   src/frontend/define.c  eq(s, d->v_name)
#       trcopy()'s formal-parameter match, the Class A site beside those
#       four: the formal's spelling on a `define` card against the body's on
#       the same card, so `define g(X) x*2` never substituted under preserve.
#       ng_ideq() now.
#       Removed 2026-08-11 with doc/claude/decisions/0013.  268 records.
#
#   src/frontend/outitf.c  strcmp(n1, n2)
#       name_eq(), beginPlot()'s answer to "is this the name the save list
#       asked for?", and doc/codex/issues/0056: byte exact in every mode, so
#       a `.save v(midnode)` against a net the deck wrote as MidNode missed
#       under preserve and killed the run, while `print v(midnode)` beside it
#       resolved.  Its four query callers call name_eq_query() now, which is
#       vec_name_eq(); the fifth caller compares two names the run itself
#       produced and keeps this comparison, classified where it stands,
#       because folding it deletes a node called Time.
#
#   src/frontend/outitf.c  strcmp(varName, d->v_name)
#   src/frontend/outitf.c  strcmp(varName, run->data[i].name)
#       OUTattributes()'s two arms, triaged with it: varName is an IFuid, so
#       both are the analysis's own name for a column against the name the run
#       stored for it -- name_eq()'s question, not the save list's -- and both
#       are unreachable today because every caller in the tree passes NULL.
#       Classified where they stand rather than left frozen, since the
#       interface is public.
#       Removed 2026-08-13 with doc/codex/issues/0056.  265 records.
#
# Format: <path><TAB><the call, whitespace collapsed>.  The line number is
# deliberately absent: keying on it would make every edit above a site look
# like a new comparison, and a contributor who learns to regenerate a baseline
# is a contributor for whom it no longer means anything.  A site that occurs
# more than once in a file appears once per occurrence.
#
# HOW AN ENTRY LEAVES.  By the comparison leaving the tree, or by its being
# classified where it stands with a `case-lint:` comment -- an annotated call
# is not a reported site, so its entry would otherwise outlive its report.
# Either way the lint fails on a baseline entry it can no longer find, so a
# rewrite of a site, and a classification of one, are both forced through this
# file and through review.  There is no expiry and no regeneration target;
# `make check` prints the exact lines to delete.  (This paragraph said "only
# by the comparison leaving the tree" until the second way was used, by
# doc/claude/decisions/0013 on eqc(ft_funcs[i].fu_name, tbuf); the ratchet is
# unchanged, because both ways go through a reviewed diff.)
#
# HOW AN ENTRY DOES NOT GET ADDED.  A new comparison is classified in the
# source instead, with a `case-lint:` comment naming the reason.  This file is
# for a comparison that is a genuine identity test and cannot be fixed yet,
# and such an entry must name the issue that will fix it.  Two are known:
#
#   src/frontend/vectors.c  cieq(v->v_plot->pl_typename, v->v_name)
#       vec_basename()'s prefix guard, doc/codex/issues/0035 item (a).  Open.
#       Not a case-mode defect -- it is an open question about what stripping
#       a plot prefix means -- but it is an identity comparison of a vector
#       name against a plot type name and it is in the frozen set.
#
#   src/frontend/variable.c  eq(copyvarname, v->va_name)   and its siblings
#       control-language variable names, byte-exact in all three modes.
#       doc/codex/issues/0048.  Mode independent and pre-existing.
#
# doc/codex/issues/0033 is NOT here and cannot be: cp_remkword(CT_VECTOR,
# name) passes the wrong string to a function, it does not compare two, so no
# lint of this shape will ever see it.  That is the measured reason this lint
# did not wait for it; doc/claude/decisions/0011-identity-lint.md decision 1.
#
# The permanent residents are worth knowing so this file is not read as debt:
# the definitions of the comparators themselves (src/misc/string.c,
# src/include/ngspice/macros.h, src/include/ngspice/stringutil.h) and the
# bodies of the six approved helpers -- ng_ideq() (inpcom.c:1074) and
# user_ident_eq() (inpcom.c:4374), ent_eq() (inpsymt.c:33), vec_name_eq()
# (vectors.c:413) and vec_wrapped_name_eq() (vectors.c:366), and
# Evt_Node_Name_Eq() (evtplot.c:63).  Those are the sites at which a raw
# comparison is the right answer, and they will never leave.
